wikipedia_extract: I-41 was an Imperial Japanese Navy B2 type submarine.  She was
  completed at Kure Navy Yard on 18 September 1943, whereupon she entered into service
  with the Imperial Japanese Navy Yokosuka Naval District, SubRon 11, and sailed to
  Yokosuka for final trials under the command of Lt. Commander Tamori Yoshimatsu.  This
  was completed by 15 December 1943 and command was transferred to Lt. Commander Itakura
  Mitsuma.  I-41 was reassigned to the Sixth Fleet in SubRon 1's Sub Division 15.
